From: daedalao <daedalao@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] PPC64 JIT: fix xsmaxdp/xsmindp encodings (SIGILL on POWER8)

PPC_xsmaxdp/PPC_xsmindp were 0xF0000400/0xF0000440, which are XX3 XO=128/136:
the ISA 3.0 xsmaxcdp/xsmincdp. The !HasPOWER9() paths of minDouble/maxDouble/
minFloat32/maxFloat32 therefore still emitted POWER9 instructions and Firefox
died with SIGILL on POWER8 as soon as JS used Math.min/max on doubles (typing
in the address bar). The ISA 2.06 encodings are XO=160/168:
  as -mpower8:  xsmaxdp vs1,vs1,vs2 = f0211500, xsmindp = f0211540
  as -mpower9:  xsmaxcdp = f0211400, xsmincdp = f0211440 (rejected by -mpower8)
Faulting word in the core dump: f0211440 (xsmincdp) on a POWER8 guest with
AT_HWCAP2=0xbe000000 (no ARCH_3_00, so HasPOWER9() was correctly false).
---
--- a/js/src/jit/ppc64/Assembler-ppc64.h	2026-09-26 10:57:28.790041814 -0700
+++ b/js/src/jit/ppc64/Assembler-ppc64.h	2026-09-26 10:57:28.808654800 -0700
@@ -777,8 +777,10 @@
   // Base (ISA 2.06) forms: NaN operands are suppressed in favor of the
   // numeric operand (minNum/maxNum style), so these are only ECMA-correct
   // once NaN inputs have been excluded.
-  PPC_xsmaxdp = 0xF0000400,
-  PPC_xsmindp = 0xF0000440,
+  // ISA 2.06 (POWER7) XX3 XO=160/168. 0x400/0x440 are XO=128/136, the
+  // ISA 3.0 xsmaxcdp/xsmincdp, which SIGILL on POWER8.
+  PPC_xsmaxdp = 0xF0000500,
+  PPC_xsmindp = 0xF0000540,
   PPC_xxbrd = 0xF017076C,
   PPC_xxbrq = 0xF01F076C,  // VSX vector byte-reverse quadword (whole 16 bytes)
   PPC_xvabsdp = 0xF0000764,
